.TH MIRRORMAN\-CLI 1 "2026" "mirrorman 0.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mirrorman\-cli \- Pacman mirror and repository manager command line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mirrorman\-cli
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mirrorman\-cli
is the command line interface of the Parch Mirror Manager.
It fetches mirror status data from the Arch Linux mirror status API,
ranks mirrors by measured response time, selects the best combination
of mirrors across countries, and writes the resulting mirrorlist to
the system.
.B mirrorman\-cli
requires a working system D\-Bus and the
.B mirrorman\-helper
service to save the mirrorlist.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS refresh
Fetch the latest mirror status from the Arch Linux mirror status API and
store the result in the local cache. If the fetch succeeds the cached
data is printed as a table unless
.B \-\-json
is given.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-country " " \fIcountry\fP
Restrict mirrors to the given country.
This option may be repeated to select several countries.
By default mirrors from all countries are fetched.
.TP
.B \-\-protocol \fIprotocol\fP
Restrict mirrors to the given protocol, either
.B http
or
.BR https .
This option may be repeated.
By default both protocols are included.
.TP
.B \-\-ipv4
Include mirrors that support IPv4.
If neither
.B \-\-ipv4
nor
.B \-\-ipv6
is given, IPv4 and IPv6 mirrors are both included.
.TP
.B \-\-ipv6
Include mirrors that support IPv6.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-status
Include mirrors that are not up to date.
By default only mirrors that report a fresh status are kept.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the fetched mirrors as JSON instead of a table.
.SS test
Measure the response time of the mirrors stored in the cache and rank
them by speed. The ranked list is written back to the cache and printed
unless
.B \-\-json
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-workers \fInumber\fP
Number of concurrent speed tests. The default is 50.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the ranked mirrors as JSON instead of a table.
.SS best\-setup
Load the cached mirrors, run the automatic multi\-country selection
algorithm, and store the chosen mirrors in the cache. The selected
mirrors are printed unless
.B \-\-json
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-count \fInumber\fP
Maximum number of mirrors to select. The default is 5.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the selected mirrors as JSON instead of a list.
.SS save
Write the cached mirrorlist to
.BR /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist
through the
.B mirrorman\-helper
D\-Bus service.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Save the mirrorlist even when no mirror is enabled.
.SS auto
Fetch the latest mirror status, run the automatic selection algorithm,
and save the resulting mirrorlist in a single step.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Save the mirrorlist even when no mirror is enabled.
.SS list
Print the mirrors stored in the cache. If the cache is empty a message
is printed instead.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the cached mirrors as JSON instead of a table.
.SS status
Show a summary of the current system mirrorlist, including whether the
file is present and how many
.B Server
entries it contains.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mirrorman/mirrors.json
Cache of the last fetched mirror data. The base directory honours
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MIRRORMAN_CACHE
Overrides the location of the mirror cache file. Mainly used by the
test suite.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for user cache files. Defaults to
.IR ~/.cache .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, for example a network failure, a missing cache, or
an unauthorized or rejected privilege request.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch mirrors from Germany, France, and Italy over HTTPS.
.PP
.RS
.nf
mirrorman\-cli refresh \-\-country Germany \-\-country France \-\-country Italy \-\-protocol https
.fi
.RE
.PP
Measure response times and save the fastest mirrors to the system.
.PP
.RS
.nf
mirrorman\-cli refresh
mirrorman\-cli test
mirrorman\-cli best\-setup
mirrorman\-cli save
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run the complete automatic setup in one step.
.PP
.RS
.nf
mirrorman\-cli auto
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mirrorman (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Parch GNU/Linux Team
